Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The program DAInf", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.45519368703125*^9, 3.4551937145625*^9}, {
   3.455448902765625*^9, 3.45544890421875*^9}, 3.4558755473125*^9, {
   3.4558880608734303`*^9, 3.4558880615140553`*^9}, 3.455960760328125*^9, {
   3.969837842695359*^9, 3.969837856121104*^9}, {3.9761660609888487`*^9, 
   3.976166061289701*^9}, {3.99282271673151*^9, 3.992822717818817*^9}},
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.8431372549019608, 0.8431372549019608, 
   0.8431372549019608],ExpressionUUID->"60c5a955-a6bb-1c46-b180-cd8b250af911"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The program works  when the object is at infinity.\n\nThis program \
has the following input  :\nrad = list of radii\nthick = list of distances \
between the  surfaces \nind = the refractive between the surfaces\ncostasf = \
aspheric constants of dioptrics\nstoprad = radius of the stop\nnstop = number \
of  dioptrics before the stop\ndis = distance of the stop from the last \
dioptric before the stop\nangle = angle between the principal ray and the \
optical axis\nwaves = wave length\norder=3 or 5 if we are interested in the \
third or fifth order aberrations.\n\nThis program is based on the DA  logic \
(Differential Algebra) , which consists of tracing a generic ray through the \
optical system, but replacing the result at each step with its Taylor \
expansion up to the fifth order. This procedure introduces errors that \
propagate through the various steps and can lead to incorrect results. The \
results improve considerably by expressing the dimensions of the optical \
system in centimeters or decimeters instead of millimeters. However, the \
program provides the aberrations evaluated in centimeters or decimeters in \
millimeters, by multiplying the results obtained by fact = 10 or 100. It is \
very important to note that the conic constants, which may characterize some \
surfaces, must not be modified in this change of dimensions. In contrast, the \
fourth-order aspheric constant must be multiplied by (10",
  FontSize->16],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["", 
    RowBox[{"-", "3"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cf4be239-86e7-834f-b349-37dd162c2e20"],
 StyleBox[") when fact = 10, and by ",
  FontSize->16],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "6"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b58de82a-6849-8446-b093-de73c5d802c0"],
 StyleBox[" when fact = 100.\nIn the examples that follow, the \
above-mentioned logic has been adopted, and the results obtained can be \
compared with those of OSLO by using the example file contained in ExsOSLO.\n",
  FontSize->16]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.45519372409375*^9, 3.455193838375*^9}, {
   3.455194346921875*^9, 3.455194379125*^9}, {3.456019290990428*^9, 
   3.456019335443553*^9}, {3.9688292916612854`*^9, 3.968829868279871*^9}, {
